<Item XName="GCSat" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>3</DataEntry>
<Description>Gain compression at saturation in dB</Description>
<DocSymbol />
<HideCondition>( GCType ~= 4 ) &amp;&amp; ( GCType ~= 5 ) &amp;&amp; ( GCType ~= 6 )</HideCondition>
<Range>[3:7]dagger.gif</Range>
<RunTimeTunable><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></RunTimeTunable>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>0</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="GCType" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>0</DataEntry>
<Description>Gain compression type</Description>
<DocSymbol />
<Enum>Amplifier__GCType@Data Flow Enums</Enum>
<Range />
<RunTimeTunable><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></RunTimeTunable>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>16</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="GComp" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>[0, 0, 0]</DataEntry>
<Description>Array of triple values for Input Power(dBm) and either Gain(dB)/Phase(deg) change from small signal or AM-to-AM(dB/dB)/AM-to-PM(deg/dB)</Description>
<DocSymbol />
<HideCondition>( GCType ~= 8 ) &amp;&amp; ( GCType ~= 9 )</HideCondition>
<Range>dagger.gifdagger.gif</Range>
<RunTimeTunable><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></RunTimeTunable>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>14</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="Gain" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>0</DataEntry>
<Description>Gain with units defined by GainUnit (used if optional voltage controlled gain input not used)</Description>
<DocSymbol />
<Range>(-inf:inf)</Range>
<RunTimeTunable><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></RunTimeTunable>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>0</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="GainUnit" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>1</DataEntry>
<Description>Gain unit for the Gain parameter or the optional voltage controlled gain input</Description>
<DocSymbol />
<Enum>Amplifier__GainUnit@Data Flow Enums</Enum>
<Range />
<RunTimeTunable><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></RunTimeTunable>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>16</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="HighInputPowerWarning" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>0</DataEntry>
<Description>Warn when input power level exceeds highest power level in compression data (meaningful when GCTYpe is &quot;Gain compression vs input power&quot; or &quot;AM/AM and AM/PM vs input power&quot;). Currently used to issue warning in RF_Link simulations with X-Parameter files.</Description>
<DocSymbol />
<Enum>Amplifier__HighInputPowerWarning@Data Flow Enums</Enum>
<IsSettable><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></IsSettable>
<Range />
<RunTimeTunable><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></RunTimeTunable>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>16</D></Validate></Item>
