<Item XName="FunctionBlock" Type="FunctionBlock" />
<Item XName="VarBlock" Type="VarBlock" /></Item>
<Item XName="Note" UserName="Note" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;FONT color=#0000ff size=6&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in; BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; PADDING-TOP: 0in&quot; class=MsoTitle align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=5 face=Arial&gt;MSR Base Station Adjacent Channel Leakage power Ratio (ACLR)&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal align=center&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: Arial; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Example Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = o ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoBodyText&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;This example demonstrates how to measure the MSR base station&amp;nbsp;Adjacent Channel Leakage power Ratio (ACLR)&amp;nbsp;according to clause 6.6.4 of 3GPP TS 37.141.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 9pt&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&gt;Adjacent Channel Leakage power Ratio (ACLR) is the ratio of the filtered mean power centred on the assigned channel frequency to the filtered mean power centred on an adjacent channel frequency. The requirement applies to frequency ranges outside the Base Station RF bandwidth. The test purpose is to &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&gt;verify that the adjacent channel leakage power ratio requirement shall be met as specified by the minimum requirement.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2 face=Arial&gt;In this example, one LTE carrier from MSR Band 14(758MHz - 768MHz) and one WCDMA carrier from MSR Band 12 (729MHz - 746MHz) are combined using SingalCombiner part. The MSR bands definition can be found in Table 4.4-1 of 3GPP TS 37.104.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2 face=Arial&gt;Equation &lt;EM&gt;TestConfiguration&lt;/EM&gt; specifies the used MSR Band and the signal configurations of each carrier e.g. sampling rate and bandwidth.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;The spectrum graph &quot;MSR_spec_Power&quot; shows the combined spectrum, while the spectrum graph &quot;MSR_spec_Power with individual spectrums&quot; shows the combined spectrum along with individual standard spectrum.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;Table &quot;ACLR&quot; shows the measured ACLR of each carrier and CACLR which are calculated in equation &lt;EM&gt;CalculateACLR&lt;/EM&gt;. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;TRY THIS:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;OL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000&gt;Change &lt;EM&gt;GCType&lt;/EM&gt; in &lt;EM&gt;Amplifier&lt;/EM&gt; in &lt;EM&gt;Design1 to add PA nonlinearities.&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000 size=2 face=Arial&gt;Change MSR bands in equation &lt;EM&gt;TestConfiguration&lt;/EM&gt; by setting F_Block1_BWlow, F_Block1_BWhigh, F_Block2_BWlow, F_Block2_BWhigh, F_BWmid.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000&gt;Change the signal configuration in equation &lt;EM&gt;TestConfiguration.&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/OL&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;</Text>
